From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_OVN_MLA_FUSEMERGE, _ABSORB_VEC, _KVB8

ai-engine 436970264 grafted onto the pin stack. MLA_FUSEMERGE fuses a chunk pass that
stops at its last live key tile with a merge that walks the row's chunks in registers;
ABSORB_VEC reads bf16 kv_b by 16-byte loads; KVB8 reads E4M3 kv_b a 128-wide load times
its scale. glm_glue_attn_ovn.cuh and glm_glue_latent_ovn.cuh carry the kernels, glue.Mla
reads the knobs at load and glue.Set carries the choice, cuda_latent.fuses picks the
fused path, and the DSA block routes through it. Default off: today's chunk programs
and merge.

Pin adaptations, each forced by the pin's own shapes: Mla.read/wanted are restored on the
pin's struct (the conflict had dropped them) with the knob set the pin actually has;
Kernels gains the new function fields and the load loop takes the source's
skipped-kernel form so unset ones carry a null handle; Set keeps the pin's fields plus
.mla; cuda_latent's headBlock takes rows alone at the pin; expandV takes `sv` at the pin
so the DSA call passes it. Comment lines single-lined.

Gates on pin+0001..0021: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new, fatbins 226/226 green.
